den-2021-a-mediocre-middle-ground/271740","site":"T Nation · 6053 posts · 2021"},{"title":"Silver and Steel","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/silver-and-steel/237353","site":"T Nation · 5418 posts · 2017"},{"title":"The Tactical Life","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/the-tactical-life/232312","site":"T Nation · 5251 posts · 2017"},{"title":"Trump 2025 - Resuming The National Nightmare Of Peace And Prosperity (Part 2)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/trump-2025-resuming-the-national-nightmare-of-peace-and-prosperity-part-2/292596","site":"T Nation · 5098 posts · 2025"},{"title":"Dodgin’ Dadbods: Fortitude Training","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/dodgin-dadbods-fortitude-training/240588","site":"T Nation · 4913 posts · 2018"},{"title":"The Return of Even More Movies You've Watched This Week III","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/the-return-of-even-more-movies-youve-watched-this-week-iii/210398","site":"T Nation · 4744 posts · 2015"},{"title":"Demigod before 35 (Aldebaran)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/demigod-before-35-aldebaran/260532","site":"T Nation · 2905 posts · 2019"}],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"The dress — Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_dress"},{"title":"Dress watch — Grokipedia","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Dress_watch"},{"title":"Watch - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Watch"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Style & presentation","chain":["Slim formal watch under the cuff","Looks refined and put together","Improves overall outfit"],"effect":"direct","text":"The watch is worn as part of a formal look. Its thin profile fits under a shirt cuff so the outfit stays clean."},"wikipedia":{"title":"The dress","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_dress"},"grokipedia":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Dress_watch","lead":["A dress watch is an elegant, minimalist wristwatch designed for formal and business attire, with a slim case, clean dial and few complications and a leather strap.[1]","Wikipedia describes traditional dress watches for business, semi-formal and formal occasions as gold, thin, simple and plain.[2] The wristwatch itself was originally mostly a women's item; men used pocket watches into the early twentieth century, and military use and the First World War popularised it.[2]","In looksmaxxing and style communities, it is treated as a finishing accessory."],"infobox":[["Type","Wristwatch"],["Case","Slim profile"],["Dial","Minimal, few complications"],["Strap","Usually leather"],["Typical use","Formal and business wear"]],"sections":[{"h":"Description","paras":["Dress watches prioritise understated refinement over sporty functionality, pairing slim cases with simple dials.[1] Some versions add a gemstone on the crown or faceted stones on the dial.[2]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"History","paras":["Elizabeth I reportedly received an \"armed watch\" in 1571, and the oldest surviving wristwatch was made in 1806 for Joséphine de Beauharnais.[2] In 1904 Louis Cartier made a wristwatch for aviator Alberto Santos-Dumont, and Cartier still sells Santos-Dumont models.[2] Rolex's predecessor, founded by Hans Wilsdorf, was an early adopter of wristwatches in the 1910s.[2]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"1806","event":"Oldest surviving wristwatch made for Joséphine de Beauharnais.[2]"},{"year":"1904","event":"Louis Cartier makes a wristwatch for Alberto Santos-Dumont.[2]"},{"year":"1915","event":"Wilsdorf's firm, which became Rolex, is incorporated as an early wristwatch adopter.[2]"}],"refs":[{"title":"Dress watch","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Dress_watch","source":"Grokipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Watch - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Watch","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Flame Free Confession III: Even More Flame Free (Part 1)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/flame-free-confession-iii-even-more-flame-free-part-1/